From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 28 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pyproject: ship the licences of the bundled libraries

The Linux wheels statically resolve and dynamically bundle HDF5, netcdf-c,
libaec, c-blosc, bzip2, zstd, OpenSSL and curl, but `license-files` names only
netCDF4's own LICENSE, so none of those projects' notices reach the wheel even
though every one of them requires the copyright notice to travel with a binary
redistribution.

Widening the entry to a glob lets the wheel build stage each dependency's
licence beside LICENSE and have it land in `.dist-info/licenses/`.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [needs a matching change in the wheel build image, which stages the files]
---
 pyproject.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ keywords = [
     "meteorology", "climate",
 ]
 license = "MIT"
-license-files = ["LICENSE"]
+license-files = ["LICENSE*"]
 classifiers = [
     "Development Status :: 3 - Alpha",
     "Programming Language :: Python :: 3",
